From 40ce3587f6922bacf0c6bbd468cea59086ad6692 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CIQ Kernel Automation <ciq_kernel_automation@ciq.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 06:52:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] smb: client: fix double-free in SMB2_ioctl() replay

jira VULN-195914
cve CVE-2026-64385
commit-author Henrique Carvalho <henrique.carvalho@suse.com>
commit f9bbadb6c94583e3b4af1afc449bfceb1d1ddec9

A response-bearing attempt can return a replayable error and free its
response buffer. If SMB2_ioctl_init() fails before the next send, cleanup
retains the previous buffer type and frees that response again.

Reset response bookkeeping before each attempt to prevent the stale free.

Fixes: 4f1fffa23769 ("cifs: commands that are retried should have replay flag set")
	Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
	Signed-off-by: Henrique Carvalho <henrique.carvalho@suse.com>
	Signed-off-by: Steve French <stfrench@microsoft.com>
(cherry picked from commit f9bbadb6c94583e3b4af1afc449bfceb1d1ddec9)
	Signed-off-by: CIQ Kernel Automation <ciq_kernel_automation@ciq.com>
---
 fs/smb/client/smb2pdu.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/fs/smb/client/smb2pdu.c b/fs/smb/client/smb2pdu.c
index 3d0627a9f6d9..e6f18e07eec0 100644
--- a/fs/smb/client/smb2pdu.c
+++ b/fs/smb/client/smb2pdu.c
@@ -3403,6 +3403,8 @@ SMB2_ioctl(const unsigned int xid, struct cifs_tcon *tcon, u64 persistent_fid,
 
 replay_again:
 	/* reinitialize for possible replay */
+	resp_buftype = CIFS_NO_BUFFER;
+	memset(&rsp_iov, 0, sizeof(rsp_iov));
 	flags = 0;
 	server = cifs_pick_channel(ses);
 
-- 
2.52.0

